0..77 Comment "// The lists of pairwise distinct naturals are an inductive-recursive family."
78..107 Comment "// The family is no universe."
108..110 Comment "//"
111..184 Comment "// A cons holds evidence of its head\'s freshness for its tail. A function"
185..257 Comment "// computes the type of that evidence from the tail. The lists and their"
258..291 Comment "// freshness thus form one block."
292..294 Comment "//"
295..369 Comment "// Freshness recurses on the list. Each arm returns the pair of two types,"
370..442 Comment "// each a call in place. The pair is data. The arm returns it as a term."
443..445 Comment "//"
446..500 Comment "// - see: the Agda standard library, `Data.List.Fresh`"
